{{Trail}}{{Notice|This page is specifically for references to the rest of the series. For clarification, this does not include things like common items found in multiple games, or the occasional reappearing character. Instead, only clear references to other events, issues, or game mechanics, which were featured in a previous entry of the series, should be included.}}{{TOCright}}
'''References''' to events in the history of ''The Elder Scrolls'' are documented here. References to things in the history of the Real World are documented separately at [[Online:Easter Eggs|Easter eggs]]. 

If you think you have found an undocumented reference, please post your idea on this article's talk page before adding it to this article. 

==[[Arena:Arena|Arena]] and [[Daggerfall:Daggerfall|Daggerfall]]==
*In the quest [[Online:Long Lost Lore|Long Lost Lore]], [[Online:Sheogorath|Sheogorath]] says that the tasks he has in mind are "Nothing so difficult as, say, reassembling the [[Lore:Staff of Chaos|Staff of Chaos]] or rebuilding the [[Lore:Numidium|Numidium]]", which were the main quests of ''[[Arena:Arena|Arena]]'' and ''[[Daggerfall:Daggerfall|Daggerfall]]'' respectively. Interestingly, the Staff of Chaos was in one piece until Jagar Tharn split it in 3E 389 and Numidium was intact until Tiber Septim activated it in 2E 896. Since ''Elder Scrolls Online'' takes place in 2E 582, Sheogorath is alluding to them being split apart in the future.
*In the quest [[Online:Wearing the Veil|Wearing the Veil]], you have to answer two riddles.  One of the possible riddles appeared in both ''[[Arena:Labyrinthian|Arena]]'' and ''[[Oblivion:The_Rosethorn_Cache|Oblivion]]'': ''Two bodies have I, two joined into one, The more I stand still the faster I run.''
*During its development, the [[ON:Thieves Guild|Thieves Guild]] questline was to take place on the island of [[Lore:Cybiades|Cybiades]] rather than [[ON:Hew's Bane|Hew's Bane]] and include the location of [[Online:Cut_Content#Thieves_Guild|Cosh Hall]]. In ''Daggerfall'', the island was somewhat of an oddity, as only one location could be found there: a [[Daggerfall:Dungeons#Human Stronghold|Human Stronghold]] called "[[Daggerfall:Ruins of Cosh Hall|Ruins of Cosh Hall]]". In ESO, the character [[ON:Cosh|Cosh]] plays an important role in the guild questline, and although the location of the DLC was changed his name was not.
* The names of the [[ON:Battlegrounds|Battlegrounds]] teams are a direct reference to [http://www.imperial-library.info/content/go-blades early designs] for ''[[Arena:Arena|TES: Arena]]''. ''Arena'' was originally conceived as a fighting game featuring a tournament that took the player to each of Tamriel's cities to challenge different gladiatorial teams. According to a file from that stage of development left behind in the final game, the Firedrakes hailed from [[Lore:Torval|Torval]], the Stormlords from [[Online:Narsis|Narsis]], and the Pit Daemons from [[Lore:Helstrom|Helstrom]]. The name of the [[ON:Blackcaster Mages Guild|Blackcaster Mages Guild]] is also a reference to these old gladiator names, being named after the Blackcasters from [[ON:Elinhir|Elinhir]].
*The [[Lore:Daggerfall Covenant|Daggerfall Covenant]]'s lion crest symbol could be a reference to the yellow lion crest that can found on some metal doors and as wall décor within the ancient ruined fort [[Arena:Stonekeep|Stonekeep]] located in [[Arena:Hammerfell|Hammerfell]] in ''Arena''. As the lion crests' poses are close to identical and that [[Arena:Queen Blubamka|Queen Blubamka]] of [[Arena:Rihad|Rihad]] referred to the ruined fortress as ancient, one can speculate the group of knights that once lived there could have been part of the Daggerfall Covenant.

==[[Redguard:Redguard|Redguard]]==
[[File:ON-costume-Swift-Winds Sailor (Saber Sparring).jpg|thumb|right|Character with both ''Redguard''-themed items equipped]]
*The [[Online:Warrior Wave Crate|Warrior Wave Crown Crates]] introduced two ''Redguard''-themed items: the [[Online:Swift-Winds Sailor|Swift-Winds Sailor]] costume, resembling [[Redguard:Cyrus|Cyrus]]'s outfit; and the [[Online:Saber Sparring|Saber Sparring]] emote, resembling that game's [Redguard:First Time Players#Combat|combat]].

==[[Morrowind:Morrowind|Morrowind]]==
* The quests [[Online:The Naked Nord|The Naked Nord]] and [[Online:If the Spell Fits|If the Spell Fits]] will both have you assisting an unfortunate Nord who was stripped and robbed by a witch. Several quests with a similar plot appeared in ''Morrowind''.
*At the [[Online:Dockyards|docks]] of [[Online:Davon's Watch|Davon's Watch]] is a ship named ''The Rusty Argonian Blade'', a reference to the pulp romance book ''[[Lore:The Lusty Argonian Maid|The Lusty Argonian Maid]]'', which has appeared in every game since ''Morrowind''.
*During the quest [[Online:Finding the Family|Finding the Family]], you will be sent to find several lost [[ON:Guar|guar]]. Two of these guar are named [[ON:Rollie (guar)|Rollie]] and [[ON:Corkie|Corkie]], a reference to [[Morrowind:Rollie the Guar|Rollie the Guar]] and [[MW:Corky|Corky]] from ''Morrowind''.
*On an island on a lake in the [[Online:Evergreen Crags|Evergreen Crags]] region in [[Online:Cyrodiil|Cyrodiil]], just south of Dragonclaw Mine, a dead [[Online:Wood Elf|Bosmer]] mage named [[Online:Icarian|Icarian]] can be found. On another island there is a ritual site and [[Online:From Nirn to the Aether|a note]], which describes Icarian's attempts to reach [[Lore:Aetherius|Aetherius]] by using magic to jump very high (obviously with catastrophic results). This is a reference to the character [[MW:Tarhiel|Tarhiel]] from ''Morrowind'', the creator of the [[MW:Scroll of Icarian Flight|Scrolls of Icarian Flight]] (seemingly named after Icarian), who can be encountered plummeting to his death near [[MW:Seyda Neen|Seyda Neen]]. The title of his notes (which are nearby), ''[[Online:From Nirn to the Aether|From Nirn to the Aether]]'', is a reference to the translation of the Daedric script on the [[Morrowind:Scrolls#Scroll of Icarian Flight|Scroll of Icarian Flight]] in ''[[MW:Morrowind|Morrowind]]'': "FROM THE EARTH TO AETHER... AND BACK". The contents of the journal also reference the scrolls with the following line: ''"They laughed when I shouted "From Nirn to the Aether and back!" from the rooftops, but I will have the last chortle."''
*During the quest [[Online:Reclaiming Vos|Reclaiming Vos]], if you talk to [[Online:Mistress Dratha|Mistress Dratha]] while she lies sick in her bed she may say ''"[[Lore:Dagoth Ur|The Sharmat]]... lurking. Waiting. Curses beneath [[Lore:Red Mountain|the mountain]]... Hear me, [[Lore:Nerevarine|Incarnate]]! Hear me."'', ''"Not now... not yet. The fire. [[Lore:House Dagoth|The unmourned house]]. Must... be ready."'', and ''"Hortator and Incarnate... must rise. I have to prepare. I have to..."'' This is Dratha foreseeing the events of ''Morrowind''.
*[[MW:Caldera|Caldera]] is referenced twice, with the [[ON:The Memory Stone|Memory Stone]] quest referring to the "Caldera Crater", the future location of [[MW:Caldera|Caldera]], and "Caldera Mushrooms", from the same location.
*[[ON:Revus Demnevanni|Revus Demnevanni]], a crazed [[ON:House Telvanni|House Telvanni]] wizard living in [[ON:Arvs-Drelen|Arvs-Drelen]] in [[ON:Gnisis|Gnisis]], is an ancestor and reference to [[MW:Baladas Demnevanni (person)|Baladas Demnevanni]], a crazy [[MW:House Telvanni|House Telvanni]] wizard living in the same location. 
*[[ON:Crew Chief Hondulf|Crew Chief Hondulf]], in [[ON:Shulk Ore Mine|Shulk Ore Mine]], makes a reference to the [[MW:Shulk Egg Mine|Shulk Egg Mine]] quest in [[MW:Balmora|Balmora]].
*In the [[ON:Mournhold Outlaws Refuge|Mournhold Outlaws Refuge]], there is a Merchant [[ON:Scamp|Scamp]] named [[ON:Creeper|Creeper]]. This is a reference to the merchant scamp of the same name.
*The [[ON:Mournhold Packrat|Mournhold Packrat]] pet is based on the [[Tribunal:Pack Rat|Pack Rat]] available in the ''[[Tribunal:Tribunal|Tribunal]]'' expansion for ''Morrowind''.
*[[Online:Barilzar|Barilzar]] makes reference to the "legendary Last Dwemer" [[Morrowind:Yagrum Bagarn|Yagrum Bagarn]] in dialogue. Yagrum is also referenced in ''[[Lore:Meet the Character - Sun-in-Shadow|Meet the Character - Sun-in-Shadow]]'' with a mention of "some blight-faced, maladjusted Dwarf".
* The [[ON:Indoril Hireling|Indoril Hireling]] encounter involves an unarmed traveler being attacked by numerous [[ON:Cliff Strider|Cliff Strider]]s. It is a reference to the high amounts of [[MW:Cliff Racer|Cliff Racer]]s in ''Morrowind'' that would swoop in and kill low-level players.

==[[Oblivion:Oblivion|Oblivion]]==
*[[Online:Darvell Litte|Darvell Litte]] is a citizen of [[Online:Chorrol|Chorrol]] who is viewed as eccentric by the other townsfolk. Much to his [[Online:Vanisande Litte|wife]]'s aggravation, Darvell claims that he can "smell" the magicka emanating from the fissure that runs through town and regrets not becoming a mage. Despite his wife's ridicule, it's clear that Darvell does have some natural competence for magic, as a descendant of his named [[Oblivion:Alberic Litte|Alberic Litte]] is a member of the [[Oblivion:Chorrol Mages Guild|Chorrol Mages Guild]] in ''Oblivion''.
*[[Online:Lisien Motierre|Lisien Motierre]] is a citizen of Chorrol who can be found in the ruins of the town's chapel. When approached, he will angrily announce that not even the gods can chase the Motierres from Chorrol. This is an ironic statement, considering [[Oblivion:Francois Motierre|Francois Motierre]]'s elaborate scheme to escape the city in ''Oblivion''.
*Another Motierre family member, [[Online:Mirabelle Motierre|Mirabelle]], appears with the [[Online:Dark Brotherhood (DLC)|Dark Brotherhood]] [[Online:DLC|DLC]]. She is a member of the [[Online:Dark Brotherhood|Brotherhood]], while the Motierres of both ''Oblivion'' and ''[[Skyrim:Skyrim|Skyrim]]'' were their clients.
*[[Online:Domitius Doran|Domitius Doran]] in Chorrol will make the claim that "500 years from now, there'll still be Dorans in Chorrol". The Doran family [[Oblivion:Jirolin Doran's House|appears]] in ''Oblivion''.
*[[Online:Governor_Fortunata_ap_Dugal|Governor Fortunata ap Dugal]], the ruler of [[Online:Anvil|Anvil]], is the ancestor of [[Oblivion:Cap%27n_Dugal|Captain Torradan ap Dugal]], an undead pirate.
*[[Online:Captain Marie Elena|Captain Marie Elena]] is a pirate captain of the [[Online:Red Sails|Red Sails]] encountered during [[Online:Dark Revelations|Dark Revelations]] in the [[Online:Enclave of the Hourglass|Enclave of the Hourglass]]. In ''Oblivion'', your [[Oblivion:A Watery Grave|first contract]] for the [[Oblivion:Dark Brotherhood|Dark Brotherhood]] sent you aboard the pirate ship ''[[Oblivion:The Marie Elena|The Marie Elena]]''.
*After committing a [[ESO:Crime|crime]], if a [[ESO:Tamriel_Guard|guard]] catches you and they start a conversation with you, they may say "Stop right there criminal scum!". This is exactly what a [[Oblivion:City_Guard|guard]] may say if they catch you and enable dialogue with you in Oblivion.
*The infamous Cliffracer Song (''"Flyyin' in the skyyyy.... cliff racer flies so high"''), sung by [[Oblivion:Aldos Othran|Aldos Othran]] in ''Oblivion'', makes a reappearance in ESO: it can be heard sung by [[Online:Valen Andrethi|Valen Andrethi]] in Davon's Watch during the quest [[Online:Exquisite Tears|Exquisite Tears]].
*A rumor in ''Oblivion'' states: ''"[[Oblivion:Dervera Romalen|Dervera Romalen]] is sure proud of the [[Oblivion:Newlands Lodge|Newlands Lodge]]. I think she's especially happy that the Red Queen drinks there."'' This line seems to relate to an [[Oblivion:Unfinished Quests#Cheydinhal|unfinished quest]] from that game. In ESO, it's possible to craft a drink called {{Item Link|quality=e|Red Queen's Eye-Opener|id=57156}}.
*The [[ON:Highland Wolf|Highland Wolf]] has a default name of "Rislav the Righteous", a reference to [[Lore:Rislav The Righteous|Rislav The Righteous]].
*The "[[Online:An Adoring Fan|An Adoring Fan]]" Achievement Furnishing is a reference to the [[Oblivion:Adoring Fan|character]] of the same name.
*The quest [[ON:A Special Request|A Special Request]] takes place partly in Anvil Castle. Part of the quest involves speaking to someone working in the castle for advice. This quest is similar in this respect to [[OB:Taking Care of Lex|Taking Care of Lex]], which also involves speaking to an insider working in the castle, who then tells you about a secret passageway to reach your destination.
*[[ON:Applewatch|Applewatch]] has three characters, including [[ON:Leono Draconis|Leono Draconis]] and [[ON:Rasala Draconis|Rasala Draconis]], a reference to its appearance in ''Oblivion'', whereby [[Oblivion:Perennia Draconis|Perennia Draconis]] resided here during [[OB:Next of Kin|Next of Kin]].
*During the [[Online:West Weald|West Weald]] storyline, [[Online:Beragon|Beragon]] mentions that the name of the last king of [[Online:Miscarcand|Miscarcand]] was [[Lore:Morimath|Morimath]]. In ''Oblivion'', you come face-to-face with the undead [[Oblivion:King of Miscarcand|King of Miscarcand]] in a section of the ruins named ''[[Oblivion:Miscarcand (place)#Miscarcand, Morimath|Miscarcand, Morimath]]''.
*The {{Item Link|Roofwater Wine|quality=0|questid=9266}} quest item from [[Online:The Last Laugh|The Last Laugh]] is a reference to [[Shivering:Bernice's Roofwater Wine|Bernice's Roofwater Wine]], a single bottle of which [[Shivering:The Paranoid Roof Watcher|can be found]] on a roof in [[Shivering:Crucible|Crucible]] in the ''[[Shivering:Shivering Isles|Shivering Isles]]'' expansion for ''Oblivion''.

==[[Books:The Infernal City|The Infernal City]] and [[Books:Lord of Souls|Lord of Souls]]==
*[[Online:Hyacinth|Hyacinth]]'s mention of a mechanical bird he built is an allusion to [[Books:Coo|Coo]], a similar device featured in ''[[Books:The Infernal City|The Infernal City]]''. 
*[[ON:Vaermina|Vaermina]]'s alternate title of Dark Lady comes up a few times, having first appeared in ''The Infernal City''.
*[[Lore:Ixtaxh Xanmeer|Ixtaxh-Thitithil-Meht]] and [[Lore:Oliis Bay|Oliis Bay]] appear in the [[ON:Murkmire|Murkmire]] zone under the same names that they were given in the novels.

==[[Skyrim:Skyrim|Skyrim]] ==
*The book ''[[Online:I was Summoned by a Mortal|I was Summoned by a Mortal]]'' contains many references to the behavior of summoned [[Skyrim:Dremora|Dremora]] in ''Skyrim'', including their habit of rushing into fights and some of their [[Skyrim:Dremora#Dialogue|battle quotes]].
*The book ''[[Online:Guard Duty|Guard Duty]]'' makes reference to the well known line of guard dialogue in Skyrim ''"[[Skyrim:Guard_Dialogue#Passing_Dialogue|I used to be an adventurer like you. Then I took an arrow in the knee...]]"'', which became a hit meme soon after ''Skyrim'''s release. 
*After completing the quest [[Online:The Coral Heart|The Coral Heart]], [[Online:Holgunn One-Eye|Holgunn]] will congratulate you with ''"Then Ebonheart is saved! We are once again in your debt. Maybe we'll make you the new Thane of Whiterun. After all, they'll take anyone!"'' This is a reference to the relative ease by which you could become the thane of [[Skyrim:Whiterun|Whiterun]] in ''Skyrim'', requiring the completion of only two quests.
*[[Online:Satuhaz|Satuhaz]], one of the bankers in [[Online:Elden Root|Elden Root]], sometimes says: ''"Satuhaz wagers, if one were to bring a pack of armored trolls to break into our vault, our trolls would be the victors in that scenario. Why, you might ask? This one has the answer: Our trolls are vampires."'' This is a reference to the [[Skyrim:Dawnguard (faction)|Dawnguard]], an order of vampire hunters known to use [[Skyrim:Armored Troll|armored trolls]] in battle.
*The quest [[ON:A Night to Forget|A Night to Forget]] is seemingly a nod to the ''Skyrim'' quest [[SR:A Night To Remember|A Night To Remember]]. Aside from the similar names, both involve retrieving items to piece together the events of a drunken night out.
*During the quest [[Online:Snow and Flame|Snow and Flame]], [[Online:Scout Snowhunter|Scout Snowhunter]] takes you to [[Online:Skuldafn|Skuldafn]] through a secret tunnel. This may be a nod to the [[Online:Dragon|dragon]] [[Skyrim:Odahviing|Odahviing]], whose name means "Snow-Hunter-Wing" in the [[Lore:Dragon Language|Dragon Language]], and who takes you to [[Skyrim:Skuldafn|Skuldafn]] during the quest [[Skyrim:The World-Eater's Eyrie|The World-Eater's Eyrie]] in ''[[Skyrim:Skyrim|Skyrim]]''.
*The merchant [[ON:Nagaddu|Nagaddu]] in [[ON:Elden Root|Elden Root]] may joke, ''"Some call this junk. This one? This one also call this junk, resell it at deep discount."'' This is a reference to a commonly-heard line of merchant dialogue in ''Skyrim'': ''"Some may call this junk. Me? I call them treasures."''
*If [[Online:Ennia|Ennia]] is spoken to, one of her greetings is: ''"Let me guess. You're looking for someplace to buy sweetrolls."'' This is a reference to the [[Skyrim:Guards|guards]] in ''Skyrim'', who sometimes say, ''"Let me guess... someone stole your sweetroll."'', making Ennia's dialogue a continuation of the gag.
* In ''[[Online:Khunzar-ri and the Demon: Part One|Khunzar-ri and the Demon: Part One]]'' it starts with one of the Khunzar-ri's exploits ''"After Khunzar-ri defeated the giant Drol by consuming four-hundred-and-one moon-sugar pies, he met a demon."'' This seems to be a nod to healing mid-battle by consuming food, which is typically stereotyped as a ridiculous amount of [[Skyrim:Food#Eidar_Cheese_Wedge|cheese wheel]]s.
*The launcher blurb during pet's debut read ''"New Inventory Pet - Let the [[ON:Explorer's Pack Donkey|Explorer's Pack Donkey]] help carry your burdens"'' is a reference to [[Skyrim:Lydia|Lydia]]'s famous line ''"I am sworn to carry your burdens."'' when trading items to store.
*[[Online:Gulfa Red-Beard|Gulfa Red-Beard]] is a Nord woman who is searching for a potion to help her grow a beard. This may be a reference to a bug in ''Skyrim'' where female draugr could sometimes possess a beard.
*The [[Skyrim:Black Book (book)|Black Book]] illustrations of crescent towers in ''Dragonborn'' are used as a reference for the [[ON:Scrawl of the Arcanist Tattoos|Scrawl of the Arcanist Tattoos]] and portals to [[Lore:Mirrormoor|Mirrormoor]] seen in [[ON:The Mythos|The Mythos]].

==[[Legends:Legends|Legends]]==
* The [[Online:Sweetroll|sweetroll]]-themed [[Online:Grisly Gourmet|Grisly Gourmet]] set from [[Online:Red Petal Bastion|Red Petal Bastion]] is a reference to the {{Card|Grisly Gourmet}} card in ''Legends'', which in turn is based on the cannibal chef [[Skyrim:Knjakr|Knjakr]] from ''Skyrim''.

==[[Blades:Blades|Blades]]==
* In ''[[ON:Ulfsild's Log: The Gryphon and the Fox|Ulfsild's Log: The Gryphon and the Fox]]'' it is mentioned that [[ON:Ulfsild|Ulfsild]] owned a paperweight made of faerite, a material which [[Blades:Faerite|first appeared]] in ''Blades''.
* When asked about [[Online:Captain Velehk Sain|Velehk Sain]], [[Online:Suraj|Suraj]] will say, ''"The destroyer, they call him. Captain of the Caterwaul. As cruel as they come in Coldharbour."'' This is a reference to Velehk's appearance in Blades, where he can be encountered as a boss-level Dremora named [[Blades:Velehk the Destroyer|Velehk the Destroyer]].

